"""
FIGURE CAPTION + ALT TEXT EXTRACTOR (accessibility-tagged PDFs)

UPDATED FIGURE NUMBER RULE
--------------------------
For every top-level <Figure> tag:

1. Figure No. is read FIRST from:
       <Figure> -> <P>/<Caption> -> descendant <Span>
   Example:
       <Figure>
           <P>
               <Span>Figure 4.1</Span>
           </P>
       </Figure>

2. Caption is still detected with the existing priority:
       a) sibling <P>/<Caption> immediately after <Figure>
       b) nested <P>/<Caption> inside <Figure>

3. If the exact nested Span hierarchy does not provide a Figure No.,
   the existing fallbacks are preserved:
       - nested P/Caption text
       - any Span in Figure subtree
       - complete Figure subtree
       - caption-derived Figure No. as final fallback

4. Alt text, page number, page labels, Excel behavior, formatting,
   warnings, role-map handling, nested Figure skipping, and update logic
   remain unchanged.

Excel output:
    Date | Chapter | Figure No. | Figure Page Number |
    Figure Caption | Figure Alt Text

Install:
    pip install pikepdf openpyxl pdfminer.six

Run:
    python figure_caption_alt_extractor.py
    python figure_caption_alt_extractor.py "D:/some/other/folder"
"""

